# Cloudflare Pages redirect rules.
#
# Rules are evaluated top to bottom; the first match wins.
#
# NOTE: this file was inert on Render (Render configures rewrites in its
# dashboard and ignores _redirects). Cloudflare Pages honours it, so the
# contents are load-bearing for the first time.

# SPA fallback: serve index.html for any path that is not a real file, with a
# 200 rather than a redirect so React Router sees the original URL. Without
# this, a hard refresh on /stock/AAPL or /community returns a 404.
/*    /index.html   200

# REMOVED: `/index.html  /community  301`
#
# That rule was harmless on Render only because Render never read this file. On
# Pages it would fire before any SPA handling and rewrite deep links to the
# community page — /stock/AAPL shared in a chat would open /community instead.
# Pages already normalises /index.html to /, so no replacement is needed.
